 "explanation": "Tempester n°50: in 16 Time Steps a pad shows and edits every note of its grid cell (Main 1.5.0.2). Before: pad k of 16 Time Steps stands for the grid cell [t, t + grid) of the selected sound, t = record +0x10 ([address] + k * 0x14), grid = [address][quantize [address]] ticks (96 48 32 24 16 12 8 8). Its LED ([routine], 13 callers, main loop) tested the 8 slots of ONE step, [routine](t) (8 ticks a step), and the pad press ([routine] case 1 -> [routine]) toggled a note at that same step. A cell spans grid / 8 steps (1/16: 3): a note in another step of the cell (recorded at a finer quantize, Time Shift) played but its pad stayed dark, and a press added a second note beside it. Docs/analyses/bugs-open-2026-11.md §7. After: SCAN tests every slot of the steps that can hold a note of the cell; a note belongs to the cell when its tick step * 8 (+4 for a half-step at step % 6 = 1, -4 at step % 6 = 5: the playback rule of [routine]) is in [t, min(t + grid, beat length)). LED: lit when the cell holds a note of the selected sound (length != 0), as before for the grid step. Press: if the cell holds such notes they are all cleared ([routine]) and the LEDs redrawn; otherwise the factory toggle runs unchanged ([routine] adds the note at the grid step). So a lit pad clears, a dark pad adds. The Beat Events screen ([routine], the other caller of [routine]) is unchanged. Cost: (grid / 8 + 1) steps * 8 slots per pad instead of 8 (1/16: 32 sound reads for a dark pad, at most 104 at 1/4); a lit pad stops at its first note. Context: main loop only (the 13 callers of [routine] are UI code). No RAM. Free flash 0x9D07A880-0x9D07AAEF (156 words), 5 words in place; [address]-[address] and [address]-[address] (the old single-step test) are no longer reached.",
